# camera-demo

PICO-Cam-A live HM01B0 preview on the ST7789V LCD. Starts capture automatically in CROP
after reset (WAIT during exposure settling, then LIVE), matching the working Waveshare demo's unscaled display window. K3
(active-low GP18) starts/stops capture. Stop places the sensor in standby and
retains the displayed image. K4 (active-low GP19) cycles CROP, NEAREST, AREA,
AREA+TIME; it works while running or paused. The top 17 LCD rows show the
state, selected mode, and button actions.

CROP selects x=0..239 and source rows 134..0 without averaging or resizing.
NEAREST selects one source pixel per destination pixel. AREA averages the
fractional source-pixel areas covering each destination pixel. AREA+TIME adds
an exponential temporal average: half the new AREA sample plus half the
previous output. Temporal averaging reduces random noise but can leave trails
on moving objects. Resizing modes use the full square 324x324 frame with the
same vertical orientation. History resets on start and mode changes. The
sensor initialization waits 10 ms after every register write, as in the
reference. Each LCD update is a complete 240x135 RGB565 transfer. Eight
startup frames are discarded on each start to give automatic exposure time to
settle; this is not a guarantee of convergence in every lighting condition. No
sensor gain, exposure, or register settings are changed by K4.

Buttons use falling-edge latches so a tap during synchronous capture is
retained. One action per press, with 30 ms of observed release before the next
press is accepted; a button held at boot must first be released. Actions take
effect between frames. Camera-linked firmware uses a 250 MHz system clock and
1.15 V core supply from startup, matching the reference capture clock but
exceeding the datasheet 200 MHz point; stopping capture retains that clock.
Capture has a 500 ms deadline. ERR3, ERR4, and ERR8 mean initialization,
capture, and standby failure; K3 retries from a stopped state. Fatal exit
codes: 2 display initialization, 5 geometry, 6 pixel/text transfer, 7 refresh,
9 GPIO/timer operation. Resources are released on fatal exits.

mm.camera.preview and tests/mm/camera/preview/preview.cpp are project code
written for modules.cpp. The default crop follows Waveshare main.c; sensor
support provenance is documented in boards/pico_cam_a/mm.mdy. The test covers
sampling, averaging history and button debounce/edge retention without camera
hardware:

```sh
sh test.sh --host tests/mm/camera/preview/
```
